Subject: [PATCH] arm64: qcom: backport SM7250 Picasso headless bring-up to Linux 6.18.58

Derived from sm7250-mainline/linux_kernel:
  base: 51e2945e2d192d40c7cad65626da03b453ab342e
  tip:  9272a06bfd3f2bb5eb952b41c70f0686a340e897

Retain original copyright/SPDX notices. See ../../SOURCES.md for provenance.
Select clocks, TLMM, RPMh, NoC and UFS. Do not backport GPU/display,
touch, audio or ADSP drivers; the local board overlay disables them.

6.18 adaptations:
- NoC uses pointer compound literals with alloc_dyn_id.
- CC driver data and CBCR arrays are mutable in the 6.18 API.
- UFS link startup notification and platform data are adapted to 6.18.
- Boot with the Picasso-specific watchdog layout (bring-up stop only).

This is not upstream and has NOT been hardware tested.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile
index dffdb21..e45a05d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile
@@ -288,6 +288,7 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_QCOM)	+= sm8250-sony-xperia-edo-pdx206.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_QCOM)	+= sm8250-xiaomi-elish-boe.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_QCOM)	+= sm8250-xiaomi-elish-csot.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_QCOM)	+= sm8250-xiaomi-pipa.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_QCOM)	+= sm7250-xiaomi-picasso.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_QCOM)	+= sm8350-hdk.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_QCOM)	+= sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_QCOM)	+= sm8350-mtp.dtb
